+# Creative Precision Fabric — executable hand wave 4
+
+Wave 4 extends the UC-native Creative Hands body from **144 to 197 executable hands** and the dynamic recipe surface from **151 to 204 callable recipes**.
+
+The direction remains unchanged:
+
+`outside creative-tool influence -> decompose behavior -> implement bounded deterministic UC primitive -> expose as hand -> compose through recipes -> verify exact execution`
+
+No external product UI, source code, branding, presets or proprietary implementation is copied.
+
+## 53 new executable hands
+
+| family | added hands |
+| --- | ---: |
+| blend / compositing | 14 |
+| raster geometry / resampling | 10 |
+| procedural raster generation | 12 |
+| audio DSP | 10 |
+| timeline finishing | 7 |
+| **total added** | **53** |
+
+The complete registry after this wave contains **197 `EXECUTABLE` hands**.
+
+## Compositing
+
+Fourteen blend hands are executable over two equal-size precision rasters:
+
+- normal
+- multiply
+- screen
+- overlay
+- darken
+- lighten
+- color dodge
+- color burn
+- hard light
+- soft light
+- difference
+- exclusion
+- add
+- subtract
+
+Each operation supports opacity and an optional precision mask. Colour output uses source-over alpha composition rather than treating transparency as opaque black. These are bounded RGBA8/sRGB operations; they do not claim scene-linear HDR compositing or every blend convention used by every DCC.
+
+## Raster geometry
+
+Ten hands provide:
+
+- horizontal / vertical flip
+- 90 / 180 / 270 degree rotation
+- crop
+- transparent or coloured padding
+- nearest-neighbour resize
+- bilinear resize
+- repeated tiling
+
+The source remains a precision raster and every output gets a new deterministic digest. Resizing is intentionally limited to nearest and bilinear in this wave; higher-order kernels remain separate future work.
+
+## Procedural raster generation
+
+Twelve generators create standalone precision rasters without an imported source image:
+
+- solid fill
+- linear gradient
+- radial gradient
+- checker
+- stripes
+- dots
+- deterministic noise
+- bounded Voronoi/cell field
+- brick
+- grid
+- rings
+- waves
+
+The general procedural raster ceiling is 4,194,304 pixels. Voronoi additionally has an explicit `pixels × cells <= 16,000,000` work ceiling so a valid-looking parameter set cannot silently produce an extreme nested-loop workload.
+
+These generators are reusable inputs for materials, masks, decals, stickers, texture stacks, UI assets and later creation recipes.
+
+## Audio DSP
+
+Ten deterministic time-domain DSP hands are added on top of the existing precision-audio body:
+
+- DC removal
+- one-pole low-pass
+- one-pole high-pass
+- static compressor
+- limiter
+- delay
+- echo
+- tremolo
+- ring modulation
+- stereo width
+
+These are useful deterministic building blocks and do not claim mastering-grade analogue models, zero-phase filtering, oversampled dynamics, spectral restoration or perceptual codec processing.
+
+## Timeline finishing
+
+Seven state-edit hands extend the existing precision timeline:
+
+- ripple delete
+- slip
+- slide
+- crossfade intent
+- opacity keyframe
+- transform keyframe
+- duplicate clip
+
+These edit `axm.precision-timeline/v1` state. They do not render final video frames or encode media. Crossfades and keyframes are explicit editable intent for downstream renderers.
+
+Ripple delete removes the selected clip, removes captions that begin inside the deleted interval, shifts later clips/captions by the removed duration, and removes transitions bound to the deleted clip.
+
+## Public surface
+
+The existing `PlatformHands.creativeHands` service remains the public entrypoint. Because its registry is dynamic, hosts automatically see the expanded body through:
+
+- `list()`
+- `get(id)`
+- `invoke(id, args)`
+- `audit()`
+- `recipeRegistry()`
+- `invokeRecipe(id, args)`
+
+No host needs knowledge of the internal module paths added by this wave.
+
+## Verification
+
+`creative-hands-wave4-selftest.js` executes representative operations from all five new families. It verifies:
+
+- the exact 197-hand / 204-recipe census;
+- blend execution;
+- geometry dimension changes;
+- deterministic procedural output;
+- Voronoi work-budget rejection;
+- real audio DSP state changes;
+- crossfade/keyframe/duplicate/ripple timeline behavior.
+
+Earlier wave proofs are updated to the same current census, so the repository cannot pass by exercising only an obsolete 86- or 144-hand body.
+
+The Python test facade runs the JavaScript proofs from the normal full repository suite. Passing CI proves the tested deterministic behavior and integration only; it is not a claim of Photoshop, GIMP, Krita, Blender, Substance, Audacity or NLE product parity.
